{"type":"message","id":"56133f8a","parentId":"791fc925","timestamp":"2026-10-17T20:33:01.311Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are performing ONE reproducible analysis of a public DNA-sequence classification task. First call describe_task. Call validate_feature once for EVERY feature family available in this run. Select a pipeline using ONLY the training-validation results: maximize validation AUPRC; for equal AUPRC maximize validation F1; if still tied prefer the simpler feature family (gc_3mer, then gc_5mer, then nt_v2_50m), then smaller C and a threshold nearer 0.5. Submit exactly ONE selected configuration using submit_pipeline. The held-out test results must never guide your feature, C, or threshold choice. Do not ask questions.\n\nFinally return ONLY valid JSON with exactly these keys:\n{\"selected_features\":\"feature name\", \"C\":number, \"threshold\":number, \"validation_auprc\":number, \"validation_f1\":number, \"heldout_auprc\":number, \"heldout_auroc\":number, \"heldout_f1\":number, \"heldout_accuracy\":number, \"interpretation\":\"one measured conclusion about this task\", \"limitation\":\"one concrete limitation of generalizing this result\"}\n\nReport numbers supplied by the tools without inventing results. A genomic-model representation is optional even if available: if it loses on validation, do not select it. Do not claim that several repetitions on one fixed dataset are independent biological tests.\n"}],"timestamp":1792269181308}}
